14425,"Halifax-Customer
The 'Balance' column shows how much money you have in your account now and the 'Available' column tells you how much you can spend today. The Available balance could contain a credit balance#160;coming in but not yet showing, and will include any agreed overdraft that you have with us. It could also take account of pending payments#160;such as debit card (POS) transactions coming out. These are items you have bought recently which are not yet showing on your statement, although the Available balance doesn't include contactless card payments that you don't yet see. If you have 350 Pound in your account with a 100 Pound overdraft, the Balance column would be 350 Pound and the Available column would be 450 Pound. You can also Check your account#160;",i04,Content Access,"GENERAL SETTINGS
