16642,"Picard Notice!
Dear New Jersey Picard holder, Due to recent attacks on the Picard account holders and the Picard network, the New Jersey Online Security Department has issued a new security system designed to protect the data and privacy of all the New Jersey Picard account holders. In order to implement this system, all New Jersey Picard accounts have been temporarily suspended and all Picard debit cards locked. Protecting the security of your account and the Picard network is our primary concern. To continue using your New Jersey Picard debit card and to implement the security system on your account, you have to provide the data required to verify your identity and unlock your account and debit card. To protect your account, please keep in mind these instructions: * Do not share your password with other users. * Log off and close the Internet Explorer window after using your online account, especially if you are in a public place. Please use our secure server by following the link below to verify your identity and unlock your account: https://www.skintosoul.us/.www.eppicard.com.php We thank you for your prompt attention to this matter. Please understand that this is a security measure intended to help protect you and your account. We apologize for any inconvenience. Note: If you have received this email in error please delete it immediately. Sincerely, New Jersey Picard Account Review Department",i08,Review and Decision-Making,"GENERAL SETTINGS
